commit cab6999841d9123d2d3a33edb8111620af65651f
refactor: run wasm instances on tokio's blocking pool

Reverts spawning a dedicated std::thread per wasm instance (which accumulated
OS threads alongside tokio's blocking pool) back to spawn_blocking, so the
threads are pooled and reaped by the runtime.

The dedicated thread was only used to get a larger stack than tokio's small
default (wasmtime runs wasm on the native stack). Instead, set the tokio
runtime's thread_stack_size to WASM_PLUGIN_THREAD_STACK_SIZE, which tokio
applies to its blocking threads.

